{"name":"Poisonous Mints","hex":"#8fd400","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"poisonous","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing sufficient poison to be dangerous to touch or ingest.","Of an animal such as a snake or spider, or parts of its body: producing a toxin intended for defensive or offensive use which is usually injected into an enemy or prey by biting or stinging; hence, of a bite or sting: injecting poison."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/poisonous"},{"term":"mints","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of mint"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of mint"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mints"}],"entries":[{"title":"Poison","blocks":[{"text":"In science, a poison is any chemical substance that is harmful or lethal to a living organism. The term of poison is used in a wide range of scientific fields and industries, where it is often specifically defined. It may also be applied colloquially or figuratively, with a broad sense."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/GHS-pictogram-skull.svg/330px-GHS-pictogram-skull.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poison","wikidata":"Q40867"},{"title":"Mint (candy)","blocks":[{"text":"A mint or breath mint is a food item often consumed as an after-meal refreshment or before business and social engagements to improve breath odor. Mints are commonly believed to soothe the stomach, given their association with natural byproducts of the plant genus Mentha. Mints sometimes contain derivatives from plants such as peppermint oil or spearmint oil, or wintergreen from the plant genus Gaultheria. However, many of the most popular mints citing these natural sources contain none in their ingredient list or contain only trace amounts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons